    "body": "### Problem\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/20e60005-81a6-48e8-963a-f7cdda6fe394\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. download the `a.txt` file below, which contains some NUL characters\n\n[a.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30777115/a.txt)\n\n2. prepare `minimal.lua`:\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"j\", \"gj\")\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"k\", \"gk\")\n\nvim.o.lines = 42\nvim.o.columns = 174\n\nvim.wo.foldcolumn = \"1\"\nvim.wo.statuscolumn = \"                     %C%s%2l \"\n```\n\n3. open a terminal window with at least 42 lines and 174 columns\n\n4. run\n\n```\nnvim --clean -u minimal.lua a.txt\n```\n\n5. press `jjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjj`\n\nthe cursor moves unexpectedly. pressing j can even cause it to jump backward.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nno cursor moving issue\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-54373e2453\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux x86_64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nst 0.8.5\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nst-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
